/usr/tests -- P32W Unix's own tests, run on P32W

    sh /usr/tests/run              all of them
    sh /usr/tests/run c basic      some parts: c lib kern basic sql sh cmd

Each prints PASS or FAIL and a count at the end (exit status 0 when all
pass). A test passes when it does on P32W exactly what it did on the
machine the system was built on:

  c/      C programs (the compiler's own tests): compiled here with cc,
          run, their output and exit status compared
  lib/    C programs that check the library with the system's help
          (stdio on files, scanf, strtol, qsort, getcwd, abort), the
          same way
  kern/   C programs that check the kernel's behaviour (signals, wait,
          open, creat, kill, stat), recorded on P32W
  basic/  BASIC programs (features, files, primes), run with basic
  sql/    an SQL script run with sql on a new database
  sh/     shell scripts (words, control flow, redirection)
  cmd/    the commands, one script each (options and edge cases), each
          run in an empty directory of its own
  video/  a C program that draws through /dev/video and reads back what
          it drew (video(4)). Not run unless asked for, as it needs the
          video card:  sh /usr/tests/run video

The expected results are the .expect files beside each test. The build
makes them (tools/mksystest.py); the host's make test runs these same
tests in the emulator.
